  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#907\", \"PowerToys#32964\", \"PowerToys#28344\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been made before. PowerToys#907 is the main ticket. It asks for a right-click context menu that changes selected text to lowercase, Title Case or UPPERCASE in any app. Later duplicates (PowerToys#32964, PowerToys#28344) were closed in favour of it, so add a thumbs-up there rather than opening a new request. PowerToys doesn't have this built in yet. A workaround that tickets #907, #40719 and #42031 mention is the community 'Change Case' extension for Command Palette (by [user], in the Microsoft Store). It transforms text without copying it into another program. An AutoHotkey script was also suggested in #907.\"}",
